// A file of global declarations plus a main() still runs main(). A top-level
// declaration keeps its place among the statements so its initializer runs in
// source order, but it is not user code: the parser must still see "no
// top-level statements" and insert the implicit main() call. Regression: an
// intermediate version of the source-order fix counted the declarations as
// statements, and this program silently printed nothing.
int counter = 3;
str greeting = "hello";

int main() {
  counter = counter + 1;
  writeln(greeting, " ", counter);
  return 0;
}
